WEBVTT

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.290
--Goddamned corpse!
--Stay down, damn it!

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:24.200
Why are you getting in my way?

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.370
--We're going after him!
--You stay here!

00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:30.290
No, I'll take him down!

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:32.080
Just stay put!

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:51.160
You idiot! Hide!

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:03.120
Kariaena Island. The city of San-Teresa.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.580
This city is the "front door" separating
the Earth and a strange other world.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:12.410
A mixture of different races and
diverse cultures, haves and have-nots...

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:16.660
But in the shadows of all this
chaos lurked countless crimes.

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:19.450
The San-Teresa Metropolitan Police maintained

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:22.330
a special unit to deal with these crimes.

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:58.000
I can't believe you just sliced him
open alone, Miss Don Quixote.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:01.660
It didn't occur to you to arrest him
so we could question him?

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:06.410
Say something!

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:09.250
He was being controlled via mildey.

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:13.330
Even if we did capture him,
we wouldn't have been able to learn anything.

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:14.540
Mildey?

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:18.250
Magic. Magic to control the dead, in this case.

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:23.790
He was devoured by evil <i>latena</i>
and turned into a living corpse.

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:27.500
So you're trying to talk your way out
of this by blaming some weird spell?

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:28.540
What?

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:30.580
You're interfering with the investigation.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:34.910
Let me guess. Somebody doesn't want
us finding out the deal with this fairy,

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:37.080
and they sent you to get in the way.

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:38.200
What are you implying?

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:40.000
What I just said.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:43.330
I don't know how much they're
paying you to do it, though.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:48.250
This is your first and last warning,
Kae Imatoeba.

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:52.080
Never insult me in that manner again.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:54.200
Next time, I'll kill you. I'm not joking.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:55.830
Oh, yeah?

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:03.870
Did the words of a lowly Earthling
like me tick you off that bad?

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:04.910
Silence!

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:05.950
Right.

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:17.500
Hey, I have a question.

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:18.450
What?

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:20.330
You're serious about arresting
whoever's behind this

00:04:20.330 --> 00:04:22.450
and getting back that fairy, right?

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:23.540
Of course.

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:25.870
Me too, actually.

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:31.200
So why are we yelling and
pointing weapons at each other?

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:37.950
Well, whatever.

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:41.120
Anyway, I hear you when you say
he was being controlled.

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:44.660
Another guy like him almost killed me yesterday.

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:47.700
What? Why didn't you say so earlier?

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:51.120
Don't ask me. I'm not your mom.

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:03.620
Kei, want to guess what I found?

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:05.500
I read the report, Cecil.

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:08.250
I want to know what they've got in common.

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:09.870
That's easy.

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:13.200
The man here, who killed your partner,

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:16.370
and this man here, who almost killed you.

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:19.330
Both of them were dead before they died.

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:21.370
I don't understand...

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:24.700
I'm talking about their blood oxygen
and lactic acid levels.

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:28.830
Both of them should've been dead
after you shot them,

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:31.160
but for some reason kept moving,

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:34.080
and then only after that did they get
the numbers a dead person should have.

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:35.830
That's what they have in common.

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:37.790
So they're like zombies?

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:41.700
I don't know. I'm not sure what
the definition of "zombie" is.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:44.160
I didn't see any signs of major drug use.

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:46.450
They both seemed to drink and smoke,

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:47.910
but both were in practically perfect health.

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:49.700
I don't know about that.

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:52.450
Um, who is this?

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:53.910
Tilarna Exedilica.

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:55.370
A knight of Mirvor.

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:59.080
Oh, a guest from the other world.

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:00.910
What's she doing?

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:04.160
Looking for magic, she says.

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:05.410
Kei.

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:08.000
Don't look at me like that.
I'm completely sane.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.540
He's the same.

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:11.620
He smells of evil latena.

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:12.870
What's latena?

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:15.540
Latena is latena.

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:18.410
Some kind of magical energy source or something.

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:19.830
I don't get it either.

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:22.950
The latena of a fairy
warped through some horrible method.

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:26.870
They ingested it on a regular basis,
and it turned them into dead men.

00:06:28.790 --> 00:06:33.580
Are you talking about a drug? From Semani?

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:37.580
Fairy dust?
These guys were regular users, right?

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:40.750
If you call the dead "regular users," then yes.

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:44.000
The Marzaney Sect has spells
that can control the dead.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.330
Well, that would explain why
it didn't show up on my tests.

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:48.580
That drug is one big mystery to us.

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:51.790
All we know is that it's made from fairies.

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:54.330
To do this to a noble fairy...

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:56.750
What terrible people.

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:59.660
So, can you use magic?

00:06:59.660 --> 00:07:01.750
It's called mildey. And I can use a little.

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:06.080
Then follow the trail of this latena stuff.
Like a police dog.

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:09.540
You seem to lack imagination, Kae Imatoeba.

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:12.200
Mildey is powerful, but not <i>all</i>-powerful.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:15.540
Pound that fact into
what little brains you have.

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:19.000
Good advice from a noble but useless woman.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:22.250
So um, are you two not friends, then?

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:25.330
If it looks that way, that's probably the case.

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:29.700
Is there anyone out there
who does like this man?

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:31.120
I see.

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:34.450
Kei.

00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:36.910
You okay?

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:39.160
I think so.

00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:42.330
Call me anytime.

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:44.450
Sure, thanks.

00:07:46.450 --> 00:07:48.080
What was that conversation?

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:49.250
Don't worry about it.

00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:52.120
No, I'm curious. Tell me.

00:07:52.120 --> 00:07:54.540
She's my ex.

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:56.000
What's an ex?

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:57.200
Shut up.

00:07:58.330 --> 00:08:01.750
The problem is when the attack occurred.

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:05.330
Either they were watching Alvarez
or there was a leak.

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:06.790
No way to tell.

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:09.250
There's any number of possibilities.

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:13.580
Oh, but you don't have to worry
about our brave knight here.

00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:16.290
She doesn't even know how to make a phone call.

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:18.200
I do too. I read it in a book.

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:22.500
Really? Wow, you're so smart!

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:24.040
Sorry.

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:27.370
Anyway, so yeah.
I'll be keeping my reports to a minimum.

00:08:27.370 --> 00:08:30.700
Sounds good. Be careful.

00:08:30.700 --> 00:08:31.870
Roger.

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:34.870
What do we do now?

00:08:34.870 --> 00:08:39.950
We do this the boring way.
But well, it's late. We'll start tomorrow.

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:41.290
I see.

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:43.370
Where are you staying? I'll take you there.

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:46.080
This is my phone number.

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:50.120
I don't want any trouble, so just go
straight to your room and go to sleep.

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:52.580
Don't worry. I'm not a child.

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:55.500
You look like one. That's why I'm worried.

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:57.500
I'm 26, you know!

00:08:57.500 --> 00:09:01.410
That's 18 in Earth years. Bye.

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:02.410
Wait!

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:12.080
It's so damn cold tonight...

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:16.370
Hello?

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:19.160
I got kicked out of the hotel.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:21.750
They say you can't bring weapons into the hotel.

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:24.000
They demanded to hold on to my sword.

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:26.330
Then let them hold on to it.

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:27.500
I can't do that!

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:30.500
To a knight, a sword is every bit
as valuable as their life!

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:33.500
Then sleep on the ground somewhere.
Not my problem.

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:34.500
Wai--

00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:49.040
Damn it all!

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:05.120
The sleeping quarters at
the police station are always full.

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:07.410
And a lot of people there don't like Semanians.

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:09.200
Sleep at my place.

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:10.620
At your place?

00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:13.620
Don't worry. I'm not going to do anything.

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:14.790
Of course not.

00:10:14.790 --> 00:10:20.330
But I don't want any rumors or scandal
or things that could hurt my honor...

00:10:20.330 --> 00:10:23.450
Then just don't tell anybody!
Shut up, already.

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:29.370
Come in. You can get your stuff later.

00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:33.200
Why are you putting that on?

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:35.120
I have a cat allergy.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:40.700
Kae!

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:43.200
Kei?

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:46.000
Oh, I meant the cat.

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:47.830
It's the word for it in my language.

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:50.080
I thought you were talking about me.

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:53.580
What's the name of that kae--no, cat?

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:54.620
Kuroi.

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:56.160
What's an allergy?

00:10:57.040 --> 00:10:59.700
I have trouble breathing when I'm around him.

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:01.750
It's a genetic thing.

00:11:01.750 --> 00:11:05.750
Then why are you keeping a cat?

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:09.370
You're full of questions, aren't you?
Give me a break.

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:22.200
About three months ago, I think it was,

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:27.250
a drug dealer that I was chasing
hit her when she was a stray.

00:11:27.250 --> 00:11:28.370
And?

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:33.290
I caught the guy, and she survived.

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:36.620
But nobody else in the department wanted her.

00:11:36.620 --> 00:11:39.080
So I'm keeping her temporarily.

00:11:39.080 --> 00:11:41.000
Even though you've got a cat allergy?

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:44.660
What else can I do?
It was partially my fault.

00:11:44.660 --> 00:11:48.040
I'm looking for someone to take her,
but with no luck.

00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:50.910
What?

00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:51.910
No...

00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:54.580
Is it that funny?

00:11:54.580 --> 00:11:58.250
I'm sorry, Kei, but this is...

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:07.620
"You're a good kitty, Kuroi."

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:12.370
Kae Imatoeba, you're more
of a softie than you look.

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:13.910
That's not it.

00:12:13.910 --> 00:12:17.790
If I threw an injured cat out in the cold,
I'd have trouble sleeping at night.

00:12:17.790 --> 00:12:19.830
I'm just doing it for myself in the end.

00:12:19.830 --> 00:12:22.700
So I'm the same as the cat, huh?

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:25.580
If you don't like it, back to the park with you.

00:12:25.580 --> 00:12:28.540
No, I'll stay here. I like it.

00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:29.910
My place?

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:32.410
No, this kae.

00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:34.750
Not you, I mean.

00:12:36.750 --> 00:12:39.830
Okay, find a place to sleep.

00:12:39.830 --> 00:12:42.580
Don't let Kuroi in the bedroom.

00:12:42.580 --> 00:12:44.250
Kei Matoba.

00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:46.830
I actually was feeling a bit lonely.

00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:49.080
"Thank you."

00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:51.660
You're welcome.

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:54.250
Um, "Good night" is...

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:56.290
"Good night."

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:57.330
That's right.

00:12:57.910 --> 00:12:59.700
"Good night."

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:15.000
She was making fun of my name

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:17.410
the whole time?

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:40.620
Did I keep you waiting, Mr. Kareem?

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:43.500
Let's not waste time, Mr. Elbaji.

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:44.750
Let's do the deal.

00:13:50.660 --> 00:13:52.620
Okay, Mr. Terrorist.

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:54.910
Cash payment is great, huh?

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:57.910
Pay us the rest when you get the goods.

00:13:57.910 --> 00:14:00.540
You seem to be doing well.

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:01.410
Yeah, I guess.

00:14:01.410 --> 00:14:06.580
Thanks to those poor fairies,
we can all live the good life.

00:14:06.580 --> 00:14:09.910
That car, for instance. It's 300,000 dollars.

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:13.540
These sneakers are 3,000 dollars.

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:16.200
But I can have a good time
with a girl for three dollars.

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:17.750
You know why that is?

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:18.540
No.

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:20.830
Because I'm hot!

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:25.290
Earth girls are all about looks.

00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:26.450
They're easy.

00:14:26.450 --> 00:14:29.330
I'm only interested in the product.

00:14:29.330 --> 00:14:31.290
Oh, sorry. Sorry.

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:32.660
Hey, Zelada!

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:36.620
You called, my lord?

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:40.580
Mr. Kareem, allow me to
introduce you to Zelada the Sage.

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:42.790
He's this wizard you were telling me about?

00:14:42.790 --> 00:14:46.330
That's right. The greatest in the world
when it comes to controlling the dead.

00:14:46.330 --> 00:14:48.160
Your words honor me, sir.

00:14:48.160 --> 00:14:53.040
I simply do what I can
for the sake of my master.

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:57.410
He said "the dead."
Does he mean users of fairy dust?

00:14:57.410 --> 00:14:59.290
Indeed.

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:05.540
My magics have not the slightest
effect on those who are pure of soul.

00:15:05.540 --> 00:15:07.500
And that's where this comes in!

00:15:07.500 --> 00:15:09.620
That's the fairy bomb?

00:15:09.620 --> 00:15:11.540
A prototype, but yeah.

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:13.870
I'm about to test it right now.

00:15:13.870 --> 00:15:15.290
What do you mean?

00:15:15.290 --> 00:15:18.040
I called them here. Using 911.

00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:20.620
I said something about suspicious
people making a ruckus.

00:15:21.500 --> 00:15:23.790
This place is off limits.

00:15:23.790 --> 00:15:26.410
--Hands above your heads, all of you!
--Don't look at the light.

00:15:34.290 --> 00:15:36.080
And it takes effect instantly!

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:38.160
What's the verdict, Zelada?

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:44.580
It worked, my lord.
The two of them are already dead.

00:15:44.580 --> 00:15:46.830
Make 'em salute, then.

00:15:46.830 --> 00:15:48.410
As you wish.

00:15:49.950 --> 00:15:51.870
Have one shoot the other.

00:15:51.870 --> 00:15:52.870
Yes, sir.

00:15:57.330 --> 00:15:59.700
Poor bastard! He's dead!

00:15:59.700 --> 00:16:02.330
Now... hmm...

00:16:02.330 --> 00:16:04.870
Make him dance on the hood!

00:16:07.450 --> 00:16:11.950
Zelada, looks like you don't
know how to dance, huh?

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:13.660
I'm sorry, sir.

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:18.000
Hilarious, huh? Huh?

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:20.250
How many can be controlled by this?

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:22.540
Five thousand? Ten thousand?
However many you like.

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:26.910
The most I've ever controlled at once is 100.

00:16:26.910 --> 00:16:28.160
What?

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:32.580
That was a prototype.
The finished product will be even more amazing.

00:16:32.580 --> 00:16:36.080
We're using the entire body of a powerful fairy.

00:16:36.080 --> 00:16:40.620
The blast radius should be...
five kilometers or so?

00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:42.790
That's the size of a nuke.

00:16:42.790 --> 00:16:46.160
We could use this to overthrow
the government of a superpower!

00:16:46.160 --> 00:16:48.330
Use it however you like.

00:16:48.330 --> 00:16:50.830
You'll have to rent Zelada too, though.

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:53.660
We'll pay.

00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:55.000
Sounds good.

00:16:55.000 --> 00:16:57.330
I'll get it ready for you,
so make sure you've got the cash.

00:16:57.330 --> 00:17:00.620
My lord, what should we do with him?

00:17:00.620 --> 00:17:02.580
Oh, take care of him.

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:45.790
It's not the first time I've been
pallbearer for a coworker,

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:47.540
but you know, it's tough.

00:17:47.540 --> 00:17:49.370
It's part of the job.

00:17:49.370 --> 00:17:55.540
The force has lost three people this month.
Morale's in the gutter.

00:17:55.540 --> 00:18:00.040
But the city council's trying
to cut our budget even more.

00:18:00.040 --> 00:18:04.250
They don't see the reality. The bastards.

00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:06.120
Chief?

00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:09.200
Never mind. Focus on the job in front of you.

00:18:15.540 --> 00:18:17.500
Are you sure you're okay?

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:18.910
With what?

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:20.540
Nothing.

00:18:20.540 --> 00:18:21.750
Let's go.

00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:26.410
Was it long?

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:27.500
Was what long?

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:30.410
Your relationship with the deceased.
You were his partner, right?

00:18:30.410 --> 00:18:33.700
Yeah, I guess. Rick was a good guy.

00:18:33.700 --> 00:18:37.870
He and I never did agree on which
baseball team to support, though.

00:18:39.450 --> 00:18:43.580
In my country, it's said that
those who are mourned by many

00:18:43.580 --> 00:18:47.450
go to a country of eternal,
peaceful spring after death.

00:18:47.450 --> 00:18:50.870
That's probably what will
happen to Detective Fury.

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:52.500
Trying to make me feel better?

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:53.830
Is that bad?

00:18:53.830 --> 00:18:55.200
No.

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:58.540
Do you know what you should
say at times like this, then?

00:18:58.540 --> 00:19:01.660
"Dasch zanna." "Thank you," right?

00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:02.750
Well done.

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:06.910
Kei, got a second?

00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:08.910
What's up, Jamie?

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:12.120
You know a patrol car went missing last night?

00:19:12.120 --> 00:19:14.870
The one from precinct 22, right?

00:19:14.870 --> 00:19:17.700
It was found in Eastrock Park.

00:19:17.700 --> 00:19:20.040
Along with two dead officers.

00:19:27.500 --> 00:19:31.500
We know that they were killed
at a construction site in Redmoor.

00:19:31.500 --> 00:19:35.330
They were brought here in their
patrol car and then thrown into the lake.

00:19:35.330 --> 00:19:37.200
You're sure it's murder?

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:40.910
From the angle of the bullet wound,
this one looks like suicide.

00:19:40.910 --> 00:19:44.870
Not sure. We'll have to wait
for the autopsy to be sure.

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:47.750
Let's have our police dog take a look...

00:19:47.750 --> 00:19:49.000
Hey, Tilarna!

00:19:53.950 --> 00:19:58.040
I'm surprised you remembered my name!

00:19:58.040 --> 00:20:00.830
Just take a look at the bodies.

00:20:00.830 --> 00:20:02.200
Bonah Tilarna.

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:03.910
That's what I told you to call me.

00:20:03.910 --> 00:20:07.250
Just take a look at this!

00:20:07.250 --> 00:20:12.330
These are dead.
Just like the assassin and the dealer.

00:20:12.330 --> 00:20:14.870
So they were regular users of fairy dust?

00:20:14.870 --> 00:20:16.290
These guys were cops.

00:20:16.290 --> 00:20:17.830
But I'm sure of it.

00:20:17.830 --> 00:20:21.500
If a cop's using, his coworkers
are gonna notice right away.

00:20:21.500 --> 00:20:23.410
Maybe they used gold jewelry.

00:20:23.410 --> 00:20:24.830
Gold jewelry?

00:20:24.830 --> 00:20:28.330
Gold jewelry can be used as a catalyst
to enhance the power of latena.

00:20:28.330 --> 00:20:30.540
But if you wanted something
with this kind of power,

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:33.120
you couldn't have a mistake
the width of a human hair.

00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:36.370
Even the best craftsmen
in my country couldn't make it.

00:20:36.370 --> 00:20:38.580
Maybe I'm wrong.

00:20:38.580 --> 00:20:39.830
No, wait.

00:20:39.830 --> 00:20:42.580
Maybe a human couldn't do it.

00:20:42.580 --> 00:20:45.290
But what about a digitally
controlled manufacturing device?

00:20:46.750 --> 00:20:49.000
Okay, there we go.

00:20:49.000 --> 00:20:50.250
What?

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:53.870
Not many people are buying
powerful manufacturing machines.

00:20:53.870 --> 00:20:57.080
I found someone using a dummy corporation. Look.

00:20:57.080 --> 00:20:58.450
Dennis Elbaji.

00:20:58.450 --> 00:21:00.870
A Semanian club owner?

00:21:00.870 --> 00:21:03.700
What the hell does a guy like that
want with a manufacturing device?

00:21:03.700 --> 00:21:04.700
Let's arrest him!

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:06.330
For what?

00:21:06.330 --> 00:21:09.160
Anything! We need to
capture him and question him!

00:21:09.160 --> 00:21:10.790
We can't do that.

00:21:10.790 --> 00:21:15.040
The Earth is ruled by a god named
"fundamental rights."

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:17.450
We need some proof to convince a judge.

00:21:17.450 --> 00:21:20.120
But we need to hurry!

00:21:20.120 --> 00:21:22.410
We need to do the paperwork.

00:21:22.410 --> 00:21:25.540
Her life is on the line!

00:21:25.540 --> 00:21:27.870
Her? You mean the fairy?

00:21:29.370 --> 00:21:31.540
Seems like this is personal.

00:21:31.540 --> 00:21:34.000
What about you, Kei?

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:38.870
Do you not care if that fiel, that fairy, dies?

00:21:38.870 --> 00:21:41.580
I feel responsible.

00:21:41.580 --> 00:21:44.540
I have my own responsibility towards her.

00:21:46.620 --> 00:21:48.160
You going to the bathroom?

00:22:05.910 --> 00:22:08.660
I thought it was more important than her life...

00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:44.700
"Next time"
Next time on <i>COP CRAFT</i>.
